 "range_audit": "No published plain-fin correlation covers Pt 60 mm / Pt/Pl 2.0 / Dc 16.3 mm (largest Pt in the plain-fin database summarised in Wang & Chi 2000 Part I Table 1 is 40 mm). The software refuses this geometry; the results below use the same Wang-Chi 2000 expressions with the range check removed, to quantify extrapolation.",
 "inputs_derivation": "Inputs (D-level):\n  geometry Sec. 2 (D0): 38 tubes (13/12/13), L 0.730 m, core 730x90x780 mm, Do 15.9, Di 14.8, Pt 60, Pl 30,\n    Fp 2.81, tf 0.2 mm, 7 circuits (5 x 6 passes + 2 x 4 passes).\n  equal-circuit equivalent (D2): 3 x 14 = 42 tubes, 7 circuits x 6 passes (water velocity and pass count of\n    5 of the 7 real circuits); reference 'area': L = 38*0.730/42 = 0.6605 m keeps total tube length/area\n    (face area -2.6 %); bound 'face': L = 0.5694/0.84 = 0.6779 m keeps face area (area +2.6 %)\n  air mass flow: Sec. 5.2 gives 670 kg/h at 0.25 m/s and 2770 kg/h at 1.03 m/s -> 2685 kg/h per m/s (D2),\n    applied to the Table 4 frontal velocities; RH not given (dry heating, D4 0.5)\n  water: 3260 kg/h (cases 1-6, D0); cases 7-9 from Table 4 velocity x 7 circuits x pi/4 Di^2 x rho (D1;\n    check 0.21 -> 895 kg/h, 0.56 -> 2405 kg/h published)\n  compared: Q_avg (Table 5), air-side dp (Table 5), and U*Ao, where U is the authors' Table 5 value\n    (U = Q_avg/(Ao F LMTD), derived by the authors from measured temperatures) and Ao is the published\n    geometry total outside area, D1: 260 fins x 2 x (0.78 x 0.09 - 38 pi Dc^2/4) + 38 pi Dc (0.73 - 260 tf).\n  Discrimination: dlnQ/dlnUA from a +-5 % UA perturbation of the model (high effectiveness hides UA error).",
